From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:30:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Import the certificate and pairing file of another
 SideStore

SideStore already hands its certificate and pairing file to other apps
through sidestore://certificate and sidestore://pairing. This lets a
SideStore built into another app, under a URL scheme of its own, take
them from a SideStore on the same device, for example the one inside a
LiveContainer+SideStore, so that it signs with the certificate the
account already uses instead of creating one or revoking it.

- ImportFromSideStore asks for both, with this app's own SideStore URL
  scheme (the URL type named "<bundle identifier>.sidestoreurlscheme")
  as the callback. It is unavailable when that scheme is "sidestore".
- URLHandler takes the answers, importcertificate and pairingfile. Each
  is confirmed by the user before it replaces anything. A certificate
  must have its private key and belong to the team this app is signed
  with.
- The onboarding's pairing file and Apple ID steps, and the Certificates
  screen, gain an "Import from SideStore" action.

